/// A channel of Go (TZ03): a queue of `capacity` items that tzroutines send to and receive from,
/// with one kind of handle for both ends. `Channel.make 0` hands each item from a sender to a
/// receiver when the two meet; a larger capacity buffers that many items. `Channel.close` closes
/// it: receivers take what is left and then get `None`, and a send traps. `Channel.share` makes one
/// more handle; the block goes with the last one. Dropping a handle never closes the channel.
record Channel<'a> { block: i64 }
instance Drop<Channel<'a>> {
    fn drop channel = Channel.__release channel
}
/// What `Channel.try_send` gives back when it cannot send now: the item, in `Full` while the buffer
/// has no room and no receiver waits, and in `Closed` when the channel is closed.
union SendError<'a> = Full of 'a | Closed of 'a
/// What `Channel.try_recv` found: an `Item`, `Empty` while the channel is open and holds none, or
/// `Disconnected` once it is closed and drained.
union Received<'a> = Item of 'a | Empty | Disconnected
